# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

This repository uses CodexFlow for Codex-native planning, implementation sessions, and project memory.

## CodexFlow Context

Read these files before planning or making substantial changes:

- `{{DOCS_PATH}}/ROADMAP.md` - current priorities and feature-tagged tasks
- `{{DOCS_PATH}}/SESSION_LOG.md` - recent work history
- `{{DOCS_PATH}}/OVERVIEW.md` - system architecture and invariants
- `{{DOCS_PATH}}/ADR.md` - architecture decisions
- `{{DOCS_PATH}}/LEARNED_PATTERNS.md` - patterns discovered during prior sessions
- `{{DOCS_PATH}}/CUSTOM.md` - project-specific conventions and gotchas

## Working Agreements

- Keep work scoped to one task or feature at a time.
- Prefer a short plan before broad edits.
- Update `{{DOCS_PATH}}/SESSION_LOG.md` after meaningful implementation sessions.
- Update `{{DOCS_PATH}}/ROADMAP.md` when task status or priority changes.
- Add an ADR entry for durable architecture decisions.
- Do not invent commands. Prefer commands documented in this repo.
- Do not read or print secrets from `.env`, private keys, credentials, or token files.

## Commands

- Test: `{{TEST_COMMAND}}`
- Build: `{{BUILD_COMMAND}}`
- Lint: `{{LINT_COMMAND}}`
- Typecheck: `{{TYPECHECK_COMMAND}}`

## CodexFlow Skills

Use these repo skills from `.agents/skills` when relevant:

- `$init-codexflow` - populate the skeleton docs from repository context
- `$plan-session` - choose the next task and produce a focused plan
- `$start-session` - begin implementation after a plan is accepted
- `$checkpoint-session` - write a handoff when context is high but the task is not done
- `$end-session` - verify, update docs, and summarize the completed session
- `$new-feature` - create a feature spec and roadmap tasks
- `$verify-codexflow` - validate CodexFlow docs and configuration

